AUDIO: 'Hello creators and creative friends. Welcome to the channel. Today I want to introduce a really useful workflow for you all. It allows you to take clothing from a reference image and transfer it directly onto a new character. Let\'s take a look at a few images I generated'

[00:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'using this method. Right now we have two images on the screen. On the left, there\'s a dress on a plain white background. This is our reference image. By using this workflow, I successfully transferred that exact dress onto a'

[00:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'young woman\'s body. Her appearance, pose, and the background scene were all generated based on my prompts. There\'s another common situation you might run into. Sometimes the clothing in a reference image is already being worn by'

[00:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'a person. You can see an example of this in the image on the left. The great thing is that this workflow can handle that situation perfectly. However, you might notice a small detail. The original model had bracelets'

[00:52] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'on her wrist, and those bracelets were actually transferred onto the new woman in the image on the right. Sometimes you just don\'t want those extra accessories in your final image. When that happens, it\'s super easy to fix. You simply need'

[01:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to cover the accessories with a solid white color. Once you block them out, they won\'t show up in your final result at all. Now, let\'s look at a few more examples.'

[01:17] [scene:talk]
