AUDIO: 'this workflow for free, just check the link in the video description below. I chose to use RunDiffusion to build this setup for a very specific reason. It comes with all the diffusion models and custom nodes I need already'

[01:42] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'pre-installed. If you don\'t know what RunDiffusion is, you can find a link to learn more about it in the description as well. This workflow is actually very straightforward. It only contains three main groups of nodes. The first group is'

[01:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'simply responsible for loading the core models. This includes our main diffusion model, the clip model, and the vein model. Once those are loaded and ready, we move on to the next step. The second'

[02:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'group handles the reference image. Its main job is to crop the photo so that only the clothing area is left. To do this accurately, it relies on a deep fashion YOLO model to automatically'

[02:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'detect the outfit. In this specific example, only a small part of the original model\'s legs were cropped out. But, if her head had been visible in the photo, the node would have cropped that out as well to keep'

[02:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the focus on the clothes. Next up, we have a node that resizes our newly cropped image to exactly 1 megapixel. This is a crucial step. If your reference image is too large, it might'

[02:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'cause some weird issues during generation. After the image is perfectly resized, it gets imported directly into the two nodes in our third and final group. I actually talked about this'

[02:56] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'exact two nodes in a previous video. In that video, I compared the image editing capabilities of Clear Chu and Flax to Client. If you want to learn more about that topic, I\'ll leave a link below.'

[03:08] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'These two specific nodes are special because they can receive images directly as inputs. Because of this, the encoding process becomes fully aware of the visual content. In our case, the system'

[03:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'knows exactly what the dress is supposed to look like. Now, let\'s check out the final output image. I placed the reference image and the new output image side by side so we can easily compare'

